From 07698b06e4868ff14faf3b80bc25d090d1f0bb60 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Wed, 29 Jul 2026 12:46:48 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 254/254] reaper v1.9.0: Device Identity Manager (Rung A - page
 + CGI + nav)

New Devices page (own left-nav section between USB Application and System
Info) correlating, per MAC, the five identity stores stock ASUS scatters:
custom_clientlist (name), dhcp_staticlist (reservation), gk_rl (access),
and DHCP leases + ARP + wireless assoclists (presence). Every action is a
read-modify-write that preserves the foreign fields of each tuple, re-reads
nvram at action time, commits, and re-runs the affected consumer - no sixth
store is introduced.

httpd do_reaper_dev_cgi (web.c, NOT MCP-gated, reuses the GK static helpers
gk_json_esc/gk_load_seen/gk_client_name/gk_rl_update): actions status /
set_name / set_reserve / unpin / set_state / widen_pool. Presence merge is
always computed from leases+ARP+assoclist (VIF-aware, MULTILAN) with seen.tsv
as enrichment only, so it works with Gatekeeper OFF. Pool math + store-budget
+ orphan/duplicate/no-lease flags computed server-side; 24h traffic enriched
CLIENT-side from the existing /reaper_traffic.cgi?f=m5 feed (no JSON parsing
in C). Registered in mime_handlers before the MCP ifdef; added to
reaper_inject.c reaper_native[].

Page Reaper_Devices.asp: inline rename (writes custom_clientlist), pool-aware
Pin modal (in-pool vs out-of-pool, recommendation flips when the pool is
tight), attention card (orphaned/duplicate reservations, pool exhaustion),
filter chips + search, Gatekeeper state per row, traffic deep-link. Handlers
wired by container id (not shared class). RDEV_00..86 seeded English into all
25 dicts (lockstep 5922; translations owed). Menu: menuTree entry +
dashboard rail item + shell ICONS glyph. langcheck gate extended to cover it.

Stock DHCP page tolerance verified: its validator checks LAN-subnet only, not
pool range, so out-of-pool reservations round-trip cleanly. Rung A = live data
only; Rung B (unified long-term storage tab on System Log) follows.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
